<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The curve <m>y = {2 x^3-3 x^2-12 x+3}</m> has stationary points at <m>x = {-1}</m> and <m>x = {2}</m>.</p><p>(a) Find the value of <m>\dfrac{dy}{dx}</m> at <m>x = {-2}</m>, at <m>x = {0}</m> and at <m>x = {3}</m>.</p><div>At <m>x = {-2}</m>: <fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/>  </div><div>At <m>x = {0}</m>: <fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/>  </div><div>At <m>x = {3}</m>: <fillin characters="5" name="ans3"/>  </div><p>(b) The stationary point at <m>x = {-1}</m> is a [ maximum point | minimum point | point of inflection ]  </p><p>(c) The stationary point at <m>x = {2}</m> is a [ maximum point | minimum point | point of inflection ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><me>\dfrac{dy}{dx} = {6 x^2-6 x-12} = {6 \left(x-2\right) \left(x+1\right)}</me></p><p>The test values <m>x = {-2}</m>, <m>{0}</m> and <m>{3}</m> lie on each side of the stationary points, and <m>x = {0}</m> lies between them, so it serves as a test value for both.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\dfrac{dy}{dx}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{24}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>0</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>0</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{24}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Sign</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>+</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>0</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>-</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>0</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>+</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Shape</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">rising</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">flat</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">falling</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">flat</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">rising</cell></row></tabular><p>(b) At <m>x = {-1}</m> the gradient goes from <m>+</m> to <m>-</m>: a maximum point.</p><p>(c) At <m>x = {2}</m> the gradient goes from <m>-</m> to <m>+</m>: a minimum point.</p><p>At a maximum point the curve rises to it and falls after it. At a point of inflection the curve flattens for an instant but carries on the same way.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>24</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-12</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>24</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>maximum point</p></answer>
    <answer><p>minimum point</p></answer>
</stack-static>